WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:08.230
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:08.230
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:13.530
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:13.530
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:18.910
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:18.910
the only thing I truly have

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:24.210
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:24.210
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:29.550
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:29.550
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.800
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.800
the season of the coming summer began.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:40.220
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:40.220
I had begun to understand many things

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:46.270
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:46.270
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:51.820
garakuta no yama kara

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:51.820
In the junk I've piled up,

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.910
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.910
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:00:55.910 --> 00:01:01.200
hibike kono koe yo

00:00:55.910 --> 00:01:01.200
Let my voice echo on.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:07.460
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:07.460
Let my heart resonate.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:13.130
namida kareru made

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:13.130
Until my tears dry up,

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:18.180
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:18.180
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:23.520
namida hareru made

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:23.520
Until my tears clear away,

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:28.520
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:28.520
though I may lose my way,

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:32.360
egakikake no ima

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:32.360
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:33.860
kizamu

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:39.620
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.150
akashi

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:39.620
kono te de

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:42.620
God.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:43.790
Please, God!

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:45.330
Please!

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:50.330
He won!

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:52.320
Three hits and a shutout.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:57.010
Powerful pitching around 100 mph, up to 102 mph.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.500
That's so great!

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.970
I've been worried about him lately, but he's done it!

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:05.140
He's finally back to full strength.

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:08.270
Shimizu?

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:10.270
H-Hi, Manager!

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.520
Your break's almost over.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:13.650
Oh, right.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:16.420
By the way, Shimizu,

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:19.520
Sakamoto had an emergency and won't be able to come in tomorrow.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:22.030
Could you cover for him in the morning?

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:24.350
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:29.000
I still have practices during summer break, so during the week I can only work nights.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.670
Oh, I see.

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:34.050
Thank you for waiting.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.360
A tall iced latte.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.170
That will be 330 yen.

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:43.040
I need to work and save up so I can go to America.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:48.060
Each Person's Summer

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:48.060
Each Person's Summer

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.060
Well, I'm off.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:54.490
A-Are you okay?

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:56.110
Did you forget anything?

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:57.510
I'm fine.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:00.260
What are you so nervous about?

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:01.510
But...

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:04.950
I'm late! Super late!

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.450
K-Kaoru?

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:14.320
Hey, good luck in your first game.

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:15.630
See you later!

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:20.050
I don't need luck.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:24.890
Morning!

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:27.490
I'm so glad I made it on time.

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:28.310
Kaoru.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.170
Are you well enough to play?

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:32.410
Yesterday you said you had a cold.

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:34.180
Yeah, I'm good.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:38.150
Well, you were better off sleeping yesterday anyway.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.330
Yeah.

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:41.590
We just did conditioning for five hours.

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:42.780
Under that scorching sun.

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:48.140
The seniors are overworking us so much just because the tournament's coming up.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:48.950
And guess what?

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:52.040
We have morning practices on the weekends too.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:02.450
This is bad...

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:05.340
I'm already busy with work on weekends.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:11.310
Shimizu?

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.740
Captain.

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:14.900
Can I talk to you for a bit?

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:16.270
Oh, sure.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.060
Are you feeling better now?

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:22.680
Yes, thank you.

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:25.240
Well, the truth is...

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:30.810
One of my friends told me she saw you working at a café yesterday.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:35.320
I'm sorry!

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:37.040
I lied about being sick.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:41.330
I scheduled that shift a long time ago and I couldn't just call in sick.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:43.170
I see.

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:47.560
I don't like lies, but I'll let this slide since you were scheduled so long ago.

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:48.750
I'm sorry.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:51.220
But you should know better.

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:56.310
Everyone's working extra hard since this is our first year at nationals.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:01.480
Shimizu, you may be a junior, but you're the second baseman.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:03.400
You need to be aware of that.

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:06.320
I'll pretend I didn't find out about this,

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:10.310
but I need you to prioritize softball over work until the tournaments are over.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:12.710
Okay, I'm terribly sorry.

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:15.420
Well, go finish warming up.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:17.540
Okay, excuse me.

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:21.800
That's not a good sign.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:24.910
She wants to go to America to cheer her boyfriend on,

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:27.680
so she's squeezing in her job whenever she has time.

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:30.270
Boyfriend? America?

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:31.570
You didn't know?

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:32.760
Shigeno Goro.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:34.170
He's a major leaguer.

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:36.320
Shigeno?!

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:39.780
Not good at all.

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:41.820
She has both talent and spirit,

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:46.920
but it's not uncommon for girls to quit because of their boyfriends.

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:51.410
Second base!

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:55.680
Nice catch, nice catch.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:56.630
Next!

00:05:56.630 --> 00:05:57.950
Okay.

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:13.190
Shibuya, relax!

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:14.640
Pitch to contact!

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:17.600
You don't need to tell me.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:29.740
Out!

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:31.030
Out!

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:31.620
All right!

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:34.080
Nice job!

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:45.630
So you see how you get an isosceles triangle here?

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:47.460
Hey, you're right.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:49.680
Okay, now try to do the rest on your own.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:51.140
Okay.

00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:57.350
Let's see, it goes like this...

00:06:58.030 --> 00:06:59.150
Man...

00:06:59.150 --> 00:07:01.970
Practicing in that heat is exhausting.

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:08.910
All right, I'm done!

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:10.360
I did it, Miss—

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:16.620
What's wrong with you?

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:19.290
I-I'm sorry, I just...

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:21.590
A job is a job even if you're a student.

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:23.710
I need you to be more responsible.

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:28.620
If something like this happens again, I'll have to find someone else!

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:32.800
Oh man, this is terrible.

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:36.230
I never thought practice would take up so much time.

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:38.720
It's so tough with two jobs.

00:07:39.190 --> 00:07:42.250
I don't know if I can keep this up.

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:43.240
No!

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:45.900
I need money to go to America!

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:48.250
I'll make it work with guts!

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:50.820
Guts! Guts! Guts! Guts!

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:53.480
Guts!

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:53.480
Sis...

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:57.780
What are you talking to yourself for?

00:07:57.780 --> 00:07:58.660
Taiga.

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:00.880
Oh, I wasn't...

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:05.080
What happened in your game?

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:08.500
Oh, about that...

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:11.420
That look! Could he have...?

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:12.910
We won.

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:15.010
Completely dominated, 4-0.

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:17.210
That was unnecessary!

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:22.950
Well, good for you.

00:08:22.950 --> 00:08:26.310
I can't have a bad start to the season.

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:29.590
If we win three more games, we'll get to play Kaido.

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:34.780
I'll give Kaido some payback for Shigeno.

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:39.970
That's a pretty cocky thing to say, Bro.

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:48.620
Yes, hello?

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:49.910
About time you picked up!

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:51.920
Kaoru, where are you?

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:55.230
Oh, Makiko?

00:08:55.230 --> 00:08:58.100
I'm lying on my bed, still dreaming.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:58.890
Huh?

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:00.370
What do you think you're doing?

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:05.290
The captain told us that there's a practice game today, didn't she?

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:24.620
Second base!

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:29.010
All right!

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:29.010
Out!

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:34.840
I-I'm so sorry!

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:38.270
I just slept in, and...

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:40.760
You didn't need to come.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:45.020
I don't know how important your job is,

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:47.350
but we don't need people who don't take softball seriously.

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:49.980
Didn't I tell you to be aware of that?

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:55.570
Don't come back until you can devote yourself to softball.

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:12.670
But we don't need people who don't take softball seriously.

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:17.840
Don't come back until you can devote yourself to softball.

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:23.060
Maybe it was never possible to work and play softball.

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:27.430
I wonder if I have to quit... softball.

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:30.850
Kaoru.

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:35.140
M-Makiko?

00:10:38.350 --> 00:10:40.450
What happened?

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:44.320
You were so excited when we made it to nationals.

00:10:45.090 --> 00:10:46.160
Well...

00:10:46.590 --> 00:10:47.870
Shigeno?

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:49.660
Yeah.

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:55.020
Until just recently, I thought I could relax if he got out of his slump,

00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:57.370
but that's not enough.

00:10:59.030 --> 00:11:02.570
It's not just that he's in America and I'm in Japan.

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:05.160
He doesn't even call or e-mail.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:08.250
I only see how he's doing through the news and the Internet.

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:12.040
It feels like he just keeps drifting farther away.

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:14.900
Like he's in a different world.

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:19.070
I want to see him.

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:28.120
I'm... going to quit the team.

00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:34.510
I want to go to America, so I can't quit my jobs.

00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:39.300
I'll just annoy the seniors if I keep playing softball.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:40.630
But...

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:43.010
L-Look at me.

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:46.600
I only joined the team because you invited me,

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:51.110
but now I can't imagine life without the team.

00:11:52.990 --> 00:11:55.470
You were practicing really hard.

00:11:55.470 --> 00:11:57.150
And you love softball!

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:59.400
You're also talented.

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:03.120
Why would you quit?

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:07.660
That's such a waste.

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:17.290
I'm home.

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:18.640
Kaoru?

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:21.510
You're not planning to get another job, are you?

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:26.290
The tutoring center called.

00:12:26.290 --> 00:12:29.770
They said they have another person looking for a tutor.

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:31.460
Oh, I see.

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:34.390
You don't have to work so hard anymore, do you?

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:39.610
You've already paid back all the money we lent you for your trip to America.

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:43.290
Oh, did I forget to tell you?

00:12:43.290 --> 00:12:47.360
I'm working so I can go there again this summer.

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:49.900
What are you saying?

00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:52.320
You have nationals next month, don't you?

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:55.290
You'll burn yourself out at this rate, you know.

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:56.980
Don't worry,

00:12:57.990 --> 00:12:59.840
I'll quit softball.

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:02.510
That's enough!

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:04.920
You're a student!

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:07.750
Stop being so immature!

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:09.350
I'm not being immature!

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:11.110
You are!

00:13:11.110 --> 00:13:13.730
You're going to quit softball to chase after a guy?

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:18.400
I didn't send you to school so you could act like trash!

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:19.650
I'm home.

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:21.590
Mom, I'm hungry.

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:26.990
What's trashy about it?

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:34.050
What's so wrong about wanting to support and be with the man I love?

00:13:34.050 --> 00:13:38.590
I'm studying anyway, so you have no right to say that!

00:13:40.390 --> 00:13:41.500
Kaoru...

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:45.690
Dear...

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:47.190
Leave her alone.

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:49.090
Wh-What happened?

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:57.850
<b>Team Resignation</b>

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:57.850
<b>Notice</b>

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:00.920
<b>Team Resignation</b>

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:00.920
<b>Notice</b>

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:09.370
I need to turn in that resignation notice.

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:11.680
Welcome to—

00:15:12.460 --> 00:15:13.630
Hey, Shimizu.

00:15:13.630 --> 00:15:14.170
Yo.

00:15:14.170 --> 00:15:16.350
Komori, Sawamura!

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:20.270
I'm glad you came near the end of my shift.

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:21.590
Did we surprise you?

00:15:21.590 --> 00:15:26.190
Komori was like "I miss talking to Shimizu."

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:27.880
Sawamura, that's what <i>you</i> said.

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:30.860
You said that we should go tease her at work.

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:34.370
You're both doing well.

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:35.860
Yeah.

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:40.460
Shimizu, you saw Honda at the World Cup in America, right?

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:41.560
Yeah.

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:43.540
You should have come along.

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:47.170
Well, I had baseball practice.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:51.710
It was still fun since the Mifune Little members all got together to cheer him on from home.

00:15:51.710 --> 00:15:52.530
Yeah.

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:56.680
Besides, Honda would just yell at me if I skipped practice to cheer for him.

00:15:57.060 --> 00:15:59.470
Wait, you didn't have practice.

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:01.510
W-Well, I guess not.

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:04.900
Sawamura, you still play football, right?

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:09.570
I quit football.

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:12.540
I messed up my knee.

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:14.930
I-I see.

00:16:14.930 --> 00:16:15.920
Sorry.

00:16:18.860 --> 00:16:21.340
Don't look so sad.

00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:23.090
I was upset too at first,

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:26.320
but I still play futsal with people at my college.

00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:27.250
I see.

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:32.050
And it's not exactly because of my knee, but I really enjoy seeing Honda taking the spotlight.

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:36.020
Since we played together as kids,

00:16:36.020 --> 00:16:41.900
seeing him play on the world stage makes me feel almost like I'm the one playing out there.

00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:43.840
Yeah.

00:16:45.670 --> 00:16:46.850
The same goes for you two.

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:50.660
You're working hard on your baseball team.

00:16:50.660 --> 00:16:53.570
And Shimizu, your softball team's going to nationals, right?

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:55.000
Yeah.

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:57.510
That's amazing.

00:16:57.510 --> 00:16:58.260
Good luck.

00:16:58.260 --> 00:16:59.680
I'll be cheering for you.

00:17:03.300 --> 00:17:04.870
Oh, Shimizu!

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:06.880
I heard you're going out with Honda!

00:17:08.890 --> 00:17:09.880
Well...

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:11.090
Good for you.

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:16.340
You've always worked hard at softball, so you can understand him.

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:19.690
You can understand his drive to reach the top.

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:22.270
And...

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:27.690
You're probably the only girl in the world who could stand to date a baseball fanatic like him.

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:28.970
Right?

00:17:28.970 --> 00:17:31.370
Seriously, good for you.

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:34.280
<b>Team Resignation</b>

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:34.280
<b>Notice</b>

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:56.220
I'm leaving.

00:17:56.580 --> 00:17:58.270
Hey, what about breakfast?

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:00.220
I'm fine.

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:02.010
I'll be late for work.

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:03.360
I see.

00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:06.850
Kaoru, Taiga's game starts at one today.

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:08.100
Can you make it?

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:09.690
Oh, yeah.

00:18:10.300 --> 00:18:12.600
I'll be going with Dad.

00:18:14.330 --> 00:18:16.490
Doesn't Dad have work?

00:18:16.850 --> 00:18:19.400
He's going to take some time off to watch the game.

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:22.130
He did the same for his first and second games,

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:27.380
since each game could be his last.

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:29.800
His last high school baseball game.

00:18:29.800 --> 00:18:31.710
He went to your games too.

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:35.410
Your last qualification game in high school.

00:18:35.410 --> 00:18:36.840
He's shy, you know?

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:40.460
So he watched and then left without you noticing.

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:45.140
You know how he used to play rugby in high school?

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:49.950
He wouldn't miss a chance to see his kids working hard in the tournaments.

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:56.830
Dad isn't against you going out with Shigeno.

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:05.290
He just doesn't want you to regret quitting softball on a whim

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:08.180
when you've been doing it since little league.

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:14.450
You only have a few more years to play on school teams,

00:19:14.450 --> 00:19:17.270
so he wants you to do it as long as you can.

00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:22.010
That's not fair, Dad.

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:25.630
You never told me.

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:41.310
Kaoru?

00:19:58.410 --> 00:19:59.220
Ball.

00:19:59.220 --> 00:20:00.720
Ball four.

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:04.410
Calm down.

00:20:04.410 --> 00:20:08.470
Don't worry, your pitches are still fast.

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:09.730
Don't give up!

00:20:09.730 --> 00:20:11.640
We have two outs!

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:15.480
Strike, batter out!

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:16.670
Take that!

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:25.720
Hit it, Taiga!

00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:27.280
A hit is a tie!

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:42.150
Go! Go!

00:20:42.150 --> 00:20:42.840
Go!

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:55.940
Out. Game over!

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:57.410
All right!

00:21:19.180 --> 00:21:20.670
He almost had it.

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:22.730
Just a few more inches...

00:21:22.730 --> 00:21:25.190
I never thought he'd cry so much,

00:21:25.190 --> 00:21:28.740
but I guess he was working really hard as the captain.

00:21:28.740 --> 00:21:29.600
Yeah.

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:35.000
Dad.

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:38.980
I'm...

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:42.420
I'm not going to quit softball.

00:21:49.730 --> 00:21:51.700
Is that so?

00:21:53.050 --> 00:21:55.740
Why don't the four of us go out for dinner tonight?

00:21:57.100 --> 00:21:57.960
Yeah.

00:22:02.160 --> 00:22:03.670
What? No way!

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:06.350
H-Honda?

00:22:06.350 --> 00:22:07.970
Is it really Honda?

00:22:09.310 --> 00:22:10.680
H-Honda?

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:12.680
Yo, you still alive?

00:22:13.480 --> 00:22:15.070
Y-Yeah.

00:22:15.070 --> 00:22:16.810
H-How about you?

00:22:16.810 --> 00:22:21.390
Well, there's been a lot going on, but I'm finally back.

00:22:21.390 --> 00:22:25.400
The Hornets are in third, and with two more wins we'll be in second.

00:22:26.850 --> 00:22:27.680
Yeah.

00:22:30.110 --> 00:22:31.440
Honda?

00:22:31.440 --> 00:22:32.490
Yeah?

00:22:32.970 --> 00:22:34.580
Do your best,

00:22:34.580 --> 00:22:36.640
and I'll do my best in softball.

00:22:53.640 --> 00:22:59.520
usubeni hikaru sora kono hoshi wa nemuranai

00:22:53.640 --> 00:22:59.520
The sky glows a faint red, illuminated by a star that never sleeps.

00:22:59.520 --> 00:23:04.900
yoake wa zutto yorisou

00:22:59.520 --> 00:23:04.900
The dawn will forever creep up on us.

00:23:05.280 --> 00:23:11.160
kimi ga doko ni ite mo nani kangaeteitemo

00:23:05.280 --> 00:23:11.160
No matter where you are, or what you're thinking,

00:23:11.160 --> 00:23:15.950
mawaru hoshi chihyou wa hitotsu dake

00:23:11.160 --> 00:23:15.950
there's only earth. One spinning planet.

00:23:16.700 --> 00:23:22.580
ikuoku mo aru yume wo mitetayo

00:23:16.700 --> 00:23:22.580
I had dreams, hundreds of millions of dreams.

00:23:22.580 --> 00:23:28.420
tsukamu kibou mitsuketa ne

00:23:22.580 --> 00:23:28.420
I finally found the hope I could hold on to.

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:34.260
ikuoku no yoru kimi to nagameta

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:34.260
The sky you and I gazed up at for hundreds of millions of nights

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:39.680
sora mo tsunagatteiru

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:39.680
is always connected wherever we are.

00:23:39.680 --> 00:23:46.150
zutto miteru dake no anohi no akogare no tame ni

00:23:39.680 --> 00:23:46.150
For the inspiration that I never lose sight of,

00:23:46.150 --> 00:23:51.400
shinjite tsuzuketa omoi wo

00:23:46.150 --> 00:23:54.870
I'll shape my life-long feelings into something tangible.

00:23:51.400 --> 00:23:54.870
zettai katachi ni suru

00:23:54.870 --> 00:23:57.330
boku to yakusoku shita

00:23:54.870 --> 00:24:03.710
The place where you and I made the promise calls out to you.

00:23:57.330 --> 00:24:03.710
ano basho ga kimi wo yobuyo

00:24:03.790 --> 00:24:07.550
sotto

00:24:03.790 --> 00:24:07.550
It gently calls out to you.

00:24:10.380 --> 00:24:15.720
Preview

00:24:10.380 --> 00:24:15.720
Preview

00:24:10.860 --> 00:24:15.690
We've been a second-rate team forever, but first place is in sight this year.

00:24:15.690 --> 00:24:17.760
Wait, Greene's hurt?

00:24:17.760 --> 00:24:20.060
Dunstan's not doing so well either.

00:24:20.060 --> 00:24:21.310
What's going to happen now?

00:24:22.140 --> 00:24:25.400
Next time, on Major: The Entrusted Dream.

00:24:25.400 --> 00:24:27.370
Run toward the stage of your dreams!

00:24:25.400 --> 00:24:29.470
Next Time

00:24:25.400 --> 00:24:29.470
Next Time

00:24:25.400 --> 00:24:29.470
The Entrusted Dream

00:24:25.400 --> 00:24:29.470
The Entrusted Dream
